From ae04d7eae9d8970040cc448973a778d861cc0ac3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:41:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0093 -- fix the yardstick: what fps counted,
 steady-state tick rate, stalls listed

40/40 plan, P0 items 2-4 (instrumentation only, no behavior change).

fps_p50/fps_p95 count RENDER PASSES (GameTimer.RenderCounter), not
frames that reached the display. Since patch 0091 Present() can skip
the blit and SDL_UpdateWindowSurface() on an unchanged frame, so the
two diverge completely on a static screen (TNP4B2: fps_p50=34.62 with
23 of 881 presents real). Adds presents_real/presents_skipped
counters at Present()'s two exits and emits them on a "fps_basis" line
beside the fps figures. Also emits which blit a real present took
(patch 0087's fast path vs the generic SDL_BlitSurfaceScaled fallback)
and the source bytes per pixel, so "does the fast blit engage at
16-bit" is read off the log rather than inferred.

tick_rate is LoopCounter / get_runtime_ms(), anchored in start_game()
after engine init but before the first room load, so a whole-run
figure folds in the pre-loop room load and any one-time stall inside a
tick. Adds a steady-state tick rate with stall ticks (>250 ms self
time) LISTED by index and duration rather than hidden, and every
component of the arithmetic printed (ticks, loop_ms, stall_ms,
preloop_ms). Tick durations are exclusive (self) time: a blocking
script call re-enters UpdateGameOnce() from inside the tick that
started it, and an inclusive measure would report each blocking walk
as one giant stall on top of the nested ticks already counted.

Adds a per-real-second cumulative series (tick, render passes, real
and skipped presents) so presents can be attributed to a PHASE of a
run -- the AGS Quest AutoPilot logs its phases against the same tick
counter.

